WEBVTT

NOTE Exported from a meeting recorder. Cues are short, like real captions,
so some sentences are split across several cues from the same speaker.

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:04.200
<v Aaron Blake>Okay, let's get started with sprint planning.

00:00:04.200 --> 00:00:09.800
<v Aaron Blake>We have two weeks, five engineers, and one public holiday on Friday.

00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:15.000
<v Jess Morgan>The top priority from product is the new billing page.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:21.300
<v Jess Morgan>Customers keep asking to switch from monthly to annual plans without contacting support.

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:28.400
<v Ken Watanabe>The backend part is mostly ready. We need an endpoint to preview the prorated price.

00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:33.000
<v Ken Watanabe>I'd estimate three days for that, including tests.

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:41.500
<v Lucia Ferreira>On the frontend, the billing page needs a redesign. The mockups are approved, so I can start on Monday.

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:47.000
<v Aaron Blake>Lucia, can you also handle the loading and error states this time?

00:00:47.500 --> 00:00:52.000
<v Lucia Ferreira>Yes, I'll include them in the same pull request.

00:00:53.000 --> 00:01:01.000
<v Jess Morgan>Second priority is the export bug. Large CSV exports are timing out for enterprise customers.

00:01:01.500 --> 00:01:09.000
<v Ken Watanabe>That one is tricky. We should move exports to a background job and email a download link when it's ready.

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:13.500
<v Ken Watanabe>I'll write a short design doc before we commit to it.

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:20.000
<v Aaron Blake>Good. Let's timebox the design doc to two days and decide in Wednesday's sync.

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:28.000
<v Priya Nair>From QA, I need the billing changes on staging by next Thursday to have enough time for regression testing.

00:01:28.500 --> 00:01:33.000
<v Aaron Blake>Noted. Ken and Lucia, please aim to merge by Wednesday evening.

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:41.000
<v Jess Morgan>Last thing, we promised the sales team a fix for the duplicate notification emails. Can someone take it?

00:01:41.500 --> 00:01:46.000
<v Priya Nair>I can take it. It's a small fix and I already know where the bug is.

00:01:46.500 --> 00:01:53.000
<v Aaron Blake>Great. That's billing, the export design doc, and the notification fix. Let's put the story points on the board after this call.

00:01:53.500 --> 00:01:56.000
<v Jess Morgan>Thanks everyone.
